{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuisHCpex55YxXR8D6rd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, as long as you're on a recent `agents` release. Two things change from the older v1 examples:\n\n- **Import path:** The v2-compatible `createMcpHandler` comes from `agents/mcp/server`, not `agents/mcp`. You install it with `npm i agents @modelcontextprotocol/server@2.0.0 zod`.\n- **Factory, not instance:** You pass it a function that builds a new `McpServer`, not a server object. The handler is stateless, so it needs a fresh server on each request.\n\nThe old path, `createMcpHandler(server)` from `agents/mcp` with `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`, is the v1 pattern. It's now called `createLegacyMcpHandler`. `McpAgent` is deprecated in favour of `createMcpHandler()`.\n\nSome Cloudflare pages and third-party listings still show the v1 code. Check which `agents` version you have installed before copying an example. I got this from the docs below and didn't test it.\n\nSources:\n- [Cloudflare handler API docs (preview)](https://ec570ea1.previews.developers.cloudflare.com/agents/model-context-protocol/apis/handler-api/index.md)\n- [Cloudflare handler API docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/model-context-protocol/apis/handler-api/index.md)\n- [Cloudflare MCP transport docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/model-context-protocol/protocol/transport/)\n- [agents@0.20.1 mcp-servers.md](https://unpkg.com/agents@0.20.1/docs/mcp-servers.md)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1201,"cache_read_input_tokens":22261,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1201},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7b43b60-fa71-419f-a566-2aaba